# Text that MUST be tokenized, with the expected kind.
#
# Format: kind<TAB>line
#
# This is the recall half of the gate. Without it, the cheapest way to make
# noise.corpus pass is to stop detecting things, which is the worst possible
# outcome for a redactor: a false positive mangles prose, a false negative sends
# PII to a third-party model.
personnummer	the number is 19850101-1234 on file
personnummer	pnr 850101-1234 confirmed
email	write to anna.andersson@example.com about it
email	forward to first.last+tag@sub.example.co.uk please
# Non-ASCII local parts. The classes were ASCII-only and Go's \b is an ASCII
# word boundary, so the name fragment egressed in cleartext beside a marker that
# helpfully carried the domain. Swedish names are this product's common case.
email	mail Åsa.Öberg@example.se today
email	mail Jörg.Müller@firma.de today
# NFD-decomposed: combining marks are \p{M}, not \p{L}, so the first Unicode
# fix still leaked the prefix on text that renders identically to the NFC form.
email	mail Åsa.Öberg@example.se today
email	mail राहुल@example.com today
email	mail nguyễn@example.com today
phone	call me on 070-123 45 67 tomorrow
phone	the office is 08-123 456 78
phone	international is +46 70 123 45 67
phone	us number 415-555-0199 works
ip	server at 192.168.1.10 responds
ip	addr 2001:0db8:85a3:0000:0000:8a2e:0370:7334 up
secret	token sk_live_51HabcdefgABCDEFG leaked
secret	anthropic key sk-ant-api03-abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz012345 pasted
secret	openai key sk-proj-abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz012345 pasted
secret	aws key AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE in the log
secret	google key AIzaSyD-abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz01234 exposed
secret	our own key ti_a1b2c3d4a1b2c3d4a1b2c3d4a1b2c3d4a1b2c3d4a1b2c3d4a1b2c3d4a1b2c3d4 pasted
secret	github token ghp_a123456789012345678901 committed
hostname	connect to crm.example.com now
hostname	host.internal is unreachable
hostname	connect to skåne-db.example.se now

# --- round-14 input classes (2026-07-30) ---
# Probed 19 shapes for the PARTIAL-LEAK failure that recurred three times on the
# email pattern (ASCII class, then \p{L}, then \p{L}\p{M}). All 19 came back
# clean, so these are here as regression pins rather than as fixes: each one
# exercises the pattern in a way no other corpus line does.
#
# Right-to-left and bidi. An RTL local part is ordinary in Arabic and Hebrew.
email	mail محمد@example.com today
email	mail דוד@example.co.il today
email	mail a‮b@example.com today
# Zero-width characters: invisible on screen, and a classic way past a pattern.
email	mail jo‍hn@example.com today
email	mail jo‌hn@example.com today
email	mail jo​hn@example.com today
# Structural embeddings: the address is real, just wrapped.
email	see https://site.test/u/anna.svensson@example.se/profile
email	{"to":"anna.svensson@example.se","ok":true}
email	From: Anna <anna.svensson@example.se>
email	click mailto:anna.svensson@example.se now
# Local-part shapes the character class has to survive.
email	mail anna+invoices@example.se today
email	mail "anna svensson"@example.se today
email	mail aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa@example.se today
email	mail anna..svensson@example.se today
# IDN, both forms. Verified equivalent: the two .example misses during probing
# were knownSuffixes refusing an unlisted TLD, not an IDN problem.
hostname	visit bücher.com today
hostname	visit xn--bcher-kva.com today
hostname	visit example.com. today
hostname	visit EXAMPLE.COM today
